WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.924
Host: Why does alveolar epithelium differ from
esophageal epithelium?

2
00:00:04.924 --> 00:00:09.937
Guide: Alveoli need a short diffusion distance
and use thin squamous cells.

3
00:00:09.937 --> 00:00:15.861
Guide: The esophagus resists abrasion with a
nonkeratinized stratified squamous lining.

4
00:00:15.861 --> 00:00:22.349
Host: A section has nuclei at different
heights, but every cell contacts the basal
lamina.

5
00:00:22.349 --> 00:00:25.043
Host: Which interpretation fits?

6
00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:33.956
Guide: Pseudostratified epithelium is
possible. In pseudostratified epithelium all
cells contact the basal lamina,

7
00:00:33.956 --> 00:00:36.881
Guide: although not all reach the surface.
